shit reverses the on-disk effects of the last shell command: a botched mv,
an rm, an in-place edit, a package install. Shell hooks bracket each command,
and a privileged helper captures pre-mutation state (kqueue plus an
LD_PRELOAD shim on FreeBSD). `shit undo` restores it.

The port installs the CLI (shit), the per-user daemon (shitd), the helper
(shit-helper), the preload shim, the shell hooks and an rc.d script.
